Implemented TASK7 room permissions, host controls, and snapshot meta across the JSON schema, Rust protocol and server, and Flutter protocol layer. `POST /rooms` now returns a `host_id` when it generates one; the CLI and Flutter room-creation flows use that identity when joining.

| Intent | `controls=host` | `controls=all` |
|---|---|---|
| `play`, `pause`, `seek`, `skip` | Host | Anyone |
| `queue_add`, `queue_remove` | Anyone | Anyone |
| `set_controls`, `lock`, `kick` | Host | Host |

A locked room refuses new valid-token joins with **4003**; bad tokens still receive **4001**. Existing guests receive `locked` for intents other than `lock`, while the host can still control the room. A kick closes the target’s connections with **4005** and removes presence; kicking oneself is rejected.

**Files:** 18 changed, spanning `protocol/room.schema.json`, Rust protocol/server/CLI code and tests, and Flutter app/protocol code and tests.

**Checks:** Rust `cargo test` passed **55 tests** (1 ignored); `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` and `cargo fmt --check` passed using the Nix-provided components. Flutter analyze passed, and Flutter test passed **28 tests** (1 live test skipped).
